  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p><strong>AWS CloudTrail</strong> is essential for auditing and compliance. By enabling CloudTrail, you ensure that every API interaction with CodePipeline is tracked, including the <b>timestamp</b>, <b>source IP</b>, AWS user, and additional context. This is crucial for audit trails and security investigations.</p><p>Another key practice is to configure <strong>Amazon CloudWatch Events</strong> (now part of EventBridge). CloudWatch Events can be used to detect changes in pipeline states or failures, triggering alerts via <b>SNS notifications</b> to the on-call team. This ensures timely operational awareness and supports automated responses.</p><p>Why the other options are incorrect:</p><ul><li><i>By using AWS CloudWatch Metrics, you can gain insights into CodePipeline's performance and status; CodePipeline metrics are available in the AWS/CodePipeline namespace, and dashboards can be created for real-time visualization.</i> – CloudWatch Metrics help with pipeline health and trends, but they do not provide detailed forensic logs about who did what, or the originating IP address of requests, which are essential for audits.</li><li><i>Enable the CodePipeline Logging setting from the management console, which allows live logs to be stored in an S3 bucket chosen by the operations team for further analysis.</i> – There is no native 'CodePipeline logging' feature that directly exports detailed audit logs to S3. The standard method for logging such activities is using CloudTrail, not a separate CodePipeline logging setup.</li></ul><p><b>Tip:</b> Always use CloudTrail for auditing API calls, and combine CloudWatch Events with SNS for proactive notifications and automation in operational monitoring.</p>",
  "query": "<p>The operations team at your organization wants to confirm that all primary AWS resources are being monitored effectively, with alerts, logs, and notifications appropriately configured. The company utilizes AWS CodePipeline as part of development workflows. To meet auditing requirements, the team needs to track details such as the timestamp of actions and the originating IP address for each activity in CodePipeline. What should the team do to ensure comprehensive logging and monitoring of CodePipeline? Select <strong>two</strong> options.</p>",
